WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-stack (90s) Narrator Hakim

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:08.854
First, information theory, game theory, and mechanism design form three altitudes of one energy-bounded computing map.

2
00:00:09.354 --> 00:00:16.691
Second, one prices bits and heat, one maps strategy, and one writes rules where honesty wins.

3
00:00:17.191 --> 00:00:19.894
Third, across every layer of computing,

4
00:00:19.894 --> 00:00:24.608
each action must clear its energy floor and pass independent checks.

5
00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:31.880
For eighty years, universities taught electrical engineering, game theory, and economic mechanism design

6
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:38.653
in separate departments with separate notation. Yet inside networked computers and multi-agent software,

7
00:00:38.653 --> 00:00:45.101
thermal noise, strategic shortcuts, and safety rules collide every single millisecond of operation.

8
00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:51.350
At ground level, Claude Shannon and Rolf Landauer price the minimum heat nature

9
00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:57.319
charges to send and erase bits reliably. One altitude higher, game theory maps how

10
00:00:57.319 --> 00:01:04.160
competing agents choose actions. At the top, mechanism design crafts rules where honesty wins.

11
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.375
On stack dot openie dot dev, this single coordinate map organizes

12
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:17.717
nine periodic tables—compute, memory, state machines, databases, communication, synthesis, formal proofs, knowledge

13
00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:24.390
claims, and goal-holding agents—pricing every design choice in real joules and microseconds.

14
00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:31.966
When software protocols measure real electricity upfront and require independent verification before commit,

15
00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:37.011
cheap bluffing stops paying off and parsimonious engineering wins every time.
